WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.501
-Republicans and right
wing pundits

00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:06.100
who support Donald Trump
have spent the last few days

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:09.000
pretending to be outraged
over a hot mic moment

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.934
in which President Biden
insulted a Fox News reporter.

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:14.300
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:21.567
Today, we're going to discuss
Republican reactions to Biden

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:24.901
calling a Fox News reporter
a stupid S.O.B. on a hot mic

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:27.234
because I'm willing to bet
anything that's going to be

00:00:27.234 --> 00:00:30.734
the biggest story in politics
for the foreseeable future.

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:32.734
-This is a
CBS News Special Report

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:34.300
I'm Major Garrett in Washington.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.067
There is breaking news
from the Supreme Court.

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:39.601
CBS News has learned
Justice Stephen Breyer plans

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:42.701
to retire at the end
of this term in June.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:46.634
-Oh, Seth, you stupid
son of a bitch.

00:00:46.634 --> 00:00:49.734
Pulled a Biden on myself. Well,
at least it works as a segue.

00:00:49.734 --> 00:00:51.667
News of Justice Breyer's
retirement

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:53.534
broke just a few hours
before this taping,

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:54.934
so I'll have more to say
about it tomorrow.

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.868
But this afternoon,
Senate Majority Leader

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:59.634
Chuck Schumer said Democrats
would confirm a successor

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.868
with all deliberate speed.

00:01:01.868 --> 00:01:04.067
And I can understand why you'd
want to have someone in place

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:05.767
before Republicans
win back Congress

00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:09.234
because as GOP reaction
to Biden's hot mic moment

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:10.801
has once again proved,
in order to be

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:13.534
a Trump supporter,
you have to lobotomize

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.734
the part of your brain
responsible for shame.

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:18.200
That's why Rudy Giuliani
always looks like

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.367
he just woke up
midbrain surgery.

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:24.334
Is this a still from
the new "Matrix" movie?

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:25.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:27.501
[ As Giuliani ] I took the
red pill and the blue pill,

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:30.567
and I got to say, still nothing
happening downstairs.

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:32.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.334 --> 00:01:33.634
[ Normal voice ] By the way,
we've used that picture

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.868
so many times it's gotten a
little dusty, hold on.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.667
And that's it.
Not even February.

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:45.300
It's our entire special effects
budget for the year.

00:01:47.501 --> 00:01:49.067
For example, here's Trump's son,

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:52.567
Eric, on Fox News last night
claiming Trump worked harder

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:55.100
than the current administration.
-These people aren't present,

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.701
they're not fighting
for this country.

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:58.634
You know the difference
between them and my father.

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:00.968
My father sat there
24 hours a day

00:02:00.968 --> 00:02:02.968
and fought for the
United States' best interests.

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:05.400
-Well, the "sat there"
part of your sentence

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.501
was the only part
that was true.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:10.934
Trump definitely sat there.
He was the king of sitting.

00:02:10.934 --> 00:02:14.567
He always had that posture like
a retired major league catcher

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:17.400
whose body just froze like that.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.033
He did that upside down
diamond thing with his hands

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:23.200
like Bizarro World Jay-Z.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.400
Trump's political superpower
was his lack of shame.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.734
There was no crime
he wouldn't commit.

00:02:26.734 --> 00:02:27.868
No lie, he wouldn't tell,

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:29.434
no matter how obvious
or brazen it was.

00:02:29.434 --> 00:02:31.567
Trump would have walked
out of the White House

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:34.934
with the bust of Abraham Lincoln
sticking out of his coat pocket,

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:36.400
if he thought
he'd get away with it,

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.667
Which he might've been able to
do since his coat looked like

00:02:38.667 --> 00:02:43.901
it was specifically made
to hide marble busts.

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:45.834
What was that conversation
like with his tailor?

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:48.400
[ Italian accent ]
Look at these beautiful lines,
we can put a Lincoln right here

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.534
a Washington right here,
no one will know.

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:52.133
[ As Trump ] You've done it
again, Giuseppe.

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:56.033
You've done it again.

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:57.634
[ Normal voice ]
And in order to support him,

00:02:57.634 --> 00:03:00.868
Trump's backers had to find ways
to convince us that they

00:03:00.868 --> 00:03:03.200
didn't know he was the con man
he obviously was.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.033
Like the way Republican
lawmakers

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:08.367
would always have conveniently
not read his tweets.

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:11.367
Or the way they kept insisting
he learned his lessons.

00:03:11.367 --> 00:03:14.133
They said this man
learned his lesson.

00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:17.167
He didn't even learn
not to hit the tweet button.

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:20.133
If there was a red dotted line
under a word.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:23.968
He would just say, "I'm pretty
sure "tap" does have two P's.

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:25.868
And on this Twitter,
we're just going to have

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:28.200
to agree to disagree."

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.467
I mean, forget Donald Trump.

00:03:29.467 --> 00:03:32.267
In the history of this nation,
no rich white man,

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:34.033
in his '70s,
has ever learned his lesson.

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:37.868
The only thing rich white men
learn is salsa dancing,

00:03:37.868 --> 00:03:40.400
and that's only if
their third wife insists on it.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:44.434
So in order to say
something as naive

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:45.801
as "Trump learned his lesson,"

00:03:45.801 --> 00:03:48.033
you have to have numbed
the part of your brain

00:03:48.033 --> 00:03:50.067
that cares if people think
you look stupid,

00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:53.467
that's clearly what's going on
in the latest fake controversy

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:55.000
surrounding Biden's outburst

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.901
that Fox News correspondent
Peter Doocy,

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:58.934
which I'm sure
you've all seen by now.

00:03:58.934 --> 00:04:01.834
But here it is anyway, just for
us all to enjoy one more time.

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:13.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:16.133
Yeah.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:23.234
Biden was muttering to himself
like he just got cut off

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:26.000
on the interstate
in his stingray,

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.701
[ As Biden ] "Look at his stupid
son of a bitch.

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:28.968
No, go ahead and merge.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.767
Definitely don't signal
or check your mirrors.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.968
You're the only person
in the whole damn world,

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:36.601
baby on board. Good luck.
Growing up, normal kid."

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:38.234
[ Normal voice ]
Now Biden's 79, okay?

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:41.067
Have you guys ever seen
two old guys greet each other?

00:04:41.067 --> 00:04:42.767
"Hey, look at his old son
of a bitch."

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:46.767
"Hey, Bert, you [Bleep] I see
you're still ugly as sin."

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:48.334
It's honestly pretty sweet,
but word of warning

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:50.434
you can jump in on that
if you're under 60,

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:53.067
they don't like that.
"Hey, grandpa, you old bastard."

00:04:53.067 --> 00:04:56.934
"What the hell did you say to
me, you little turd?!"

00:04:56.934 --> 00:04:59.601
And look, ideally, the president
would not lob insults

00:04:59.601 --> 00:05:01.067
at anyone, including reporters.

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:04.367
But if we're being honest,
you know?

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:05.767
It was kind of
a stupid question.

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:07.534
I mean, really,

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:10.834
does Biden think inflation
is a political liability?

00:05:10.834 --> 00:05:12.701
What's he supposed to say?
"No. No.

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:15.667
I think it's good that gas and
ground beef are more expensive.

00:05:15.667 --> 00:05:17.534
I'm going to cruise
to reelection

00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:21.634
on the strength of Subway's
$6 foot long."

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:25.968
Anyway, all in all, I do have to
say both Doocy and Biden

00:05:25.968 --> 00:05:27.334
have handled this incident well.

00:05:27.334 --> 00:05:30.167
Doocy laughed it off,
said he wasn't owed an apology,

00:05:30.167 --> 00:05:31.767
and Biden called him
to tell him,

00:05:31.767 --> 00:05:34.734
"It's nothing personal, pal,"
which does strike me

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.300
as kind
of a non-apology apology.

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.267
You called him
a stupid son of a bitch.

00:05:38.267 --> 00:05:41.367
If it wasn't personal,
then what was it, business?

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:42.734
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:44.534
That's how we seal
the deal in Scranton.

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:46.200
You agree to the term
shake hands,

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.367
look each other in the eye
and say,

00:05:47.367 --> 00:05:48.701
"You stupid son of a bitch."

00:05:48.701 --> 00:05:50.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.934 --> 00:05:54.267
But let's just get the false
equivalency out of the way.

00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:56.467
No, this isn't even
remotely like Trump,

00:05:56.467 --> 00:05:59.000
who repeatedly whipped
his crazed fans

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:01.200
into a frenzy
by hurling insults at reporters

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:02.901
and calling them
the enemy of the people.

00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:05.901
Calling one person an S.O.B.
and then apologizing for it

00:06:05.901 --> 00:06:08.267
is not the same
as unrepentantly hurling

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:10.534
a constant stream
of verbal abuse of reporters

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:12.133
and threatening to punish
or imprison them

00:06:12.133 --> 00:06:14.400
or change
the laws to target them.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.601
I could give countless
examples of this,

00:06:16.601 --> 00:06:19.467
but here's just one random one
I happen to like.

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:23.400
When Trump called a reporter
a criminal in 2020

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.300
for not reporting
on his deranged conspiracy

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:27.200
theories about the Biden family
during the election.

00:06:32.234 --> 00:06:34.033
-He is a criminal.
He's a criminal.

00:06:34.033 --> 00:06:36.567
He got caught.
Read his laptop.

00:06:36.567 --> 00:06:37.767
And you know who's a criminal?

00:06:37.767 --> 00:06:39.834
You're a criminal
for not reporting it.

00:06:39.834 --> 00:06:42.767
You are a criminal
for not reporting it.

00:06:42.767 --> 00:06:44.267
Let me tell you something.

00:06:44.267 --> 00:06:46.601
Joe Biden is a criminal
and he's been a criminal

00:06:46.601 --> 00:06:48.701
for a long time
and you're a criminal

00:06:48.701 --> 00:06:50.767
and the media
for not reporting it.

00:06:50.767 --> 00:06:52.501
Good luck.
Everybody have a good time.

00:06:52.501 --> 00:06:57.567
Now, you can't tell them
to have a good time

00:06:57.567 --> 00:07:01.467
after you call them criminals.
The only way that works

00:07:01.467 --> 00:07:04.133
is you're at the Legion
of Doom Christmas party.

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:06.133
[ As Lex Luthor ] This is the
largest gathering of criminals,

00:07:06.133 --> 00:07:09.601
lowlife, and evil villains
the world has ever known.

00:07:09.601 --> 00:07:11.767
Have a good time.

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:13.434
Don't forget to put your Secret
Santa gifts

00:07:13.434 --> 00:07:15.434
on the table
by the alligator pit.

00:07:18.801 --> 00:07:20.133
[ Normal voice ]
That was always Trump's way of

00:07:20.133 --> 00:07:22.501
just erasing everything
he said right before it.

00:07:22.501 --> 00:07:23.767
"Have a good time."

00:07:23.767 --> 00:07:26.067
Like he'd be in
the middle of a terrifying rant

00:07:26.067 --> 00:07:28.501
where he threatens nuclear
annihilation with North Korea.

00:07:28.501 --> 00:07:30.200
And then he'd wrap it up
by saying,

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:33.100
"So, if we have to burn this guy
and turn the world to ash,

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:36.300
I will summon God's vengeance
and rain blood

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:37.601
down upon my enemies.

00:07:37.601 --> 00:07:40.167
But for now,
you have a good time."

00:07:40.167 --> 00:07:41.834
You know, because he'd be in the
middle of a wedding toast

00:07:41.834 --> 00:07:43.801
at Mar-a-Lago.

00:07:43.801 --> 00:07:46.567
You may now kiss the bride,
before she's a pile of ash.

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:50.467
So Trump's record on this
is obvious

00:07:50.467 --> 00:07:52.834
to anyone who's been awake
for the last few years.

00:07:52.834 --> 00:07:54.300
And yet there still
some Republicans

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:56.634
who think we were all born
within the last 12 months

00:07:56.634 --> 00:07:58.767
and have no memory of what Trump
was like as president.

00:07:58.767 --> 00:08:01.267
For example,
Indiana Congressman Jim Banks

00:08:01.267 --> 00:08:03.701
tweeted in total sincerity,
not as a joke.

00:08:03.701 --> 00:08:06.801
"Have we ever seen a president
attack and malign

00:08:06.801 --> 00:08:10.601
the free press
like Joe Biden has?"

00:08:10.601 --> 00:08:12.200
Only one or two things
can be happening here,

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.601
either he's trolling us

00:08:13.601 --> 00:08:15.434
because Trump's record
of antagonism toward the press

00:08:15.434 --> 00:08:17.167
is so obvious
that he knows a comment

00:08:17.167 --> 00:08:19.133
like that will drive
the rest of us insane.

00:08:19.133 --> 00:08:22.234
Or he's got some sort of
Benjamin Button disease

00:08:22.234 --> 00:08:24.634
where he looks like
a middle aged man,

00:08:24.634 --> 00:08:26.534
but was actually born
like a few months ago

00:08:26.534 --> 00:08:29.067
and legitimately doesn't know
who Donald Trump is.

00:08:29.067 --> 00:08:32.100
And if that's the case,
good on him.

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:34.033
I mean, if congressman
Banks really is a baby

00:08:34.033 --> 00:08:36.400
who looks like a full grown man
who am I to [Bleep] all over him

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:39.133
for being dumb
as a bag of rocks?

00:08:39.133 --> 00:08:40.634
I have a baby at home.
She didn't do anything.

00:08:40.634 --> 00:08:42.200
But this baby
is out here not letting

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.767
Benjamin Button disease
slow him down,

00:08:43.767 --> 00:08:46.000
serving his constituents.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:47.934
Go to work every day
with people who all

00:08:47.934 --> 00:08:50.667
have faces
that are terrifying to babies.

00:08:50.667 --> 00:08:52.100
He's going to talk
to these people,

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:54.200
and I burst into tears, probably
as a full diaper half the day.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:57.534
So again, if Congressman Banks
is a Benjamin Button situation,

00:08:57.534 --> 00:08:59.067
and that's why he doesn't
remember how Donald Trump

00:08:59.067 --> 00:09:00.767
treated the press, I apologize.

00:09:00.767 --> 00:09:03.968
But you know, if he is just a
regular 42-year-old man,

00:09:03.968 --> 00:09:06.901
you know, shut the [Bleep] up.

00:09:06.901 --> 00:09:09.167
But that was somehow not,
that was somehow not

00:09:09.167 --> 00:09:10.667
the most disingenuous reaction

00:09:10.667 --> 00:09:12.167
from a Republican
member of Congress.

00:09:12.167 --> 00:09:13.701
There was also Ronny Jackson,

00:09:13.701 --> 00:09:16.367
Trump's former doctor, who
claimed in 2018,

00:09:16.367 --> 00:09:17.934
that Trump aced
the cognitive test.

00:09:17.934 --> 00:09:20.067
Jackson said on
Fox News yesterday

00:09:20.067 --> 00:09:23.901
that Biden's hot mic moment
was a sign of cognitive decline.

00:09:23.901 --> 00:09:26.167
-It's completely unprofessional.
It's embarrassing.

00:09:26.167 --> 00:09:27.567
And I've seen
this multiple times

00:09:27.567 --> 00:09:29.367
with people
at the president's age

00:09:29.367 --> 00:09:31.100
that are starting to have
cognitive issues.

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:33.868
They get short tempered, they
get irritable, they strike out.

00:09:33.868 --> 00:09:36.067
It's a defense mechanism to some
extent when they don't know

00:09:36.067 --> 00:09:38.567
exactly how to answer questions
or what's going on around them.

00:09:38.567 --> 00:09:40.767
He's got cognitive issues.
He's not fit to be our head --

00:09:40.767 --> 00:09:43.968
head of state
or our commander in chief.

00:09:43.968 --> 00:09:45.767
-Now, yes, he's a doctor,
but remember,

00:09:45.767 --> 00:09:49.300
he's a doctor
whose name is Ronny.

00:09:49.300 --> 00:09:50.734
Now, do you have
your medical degree?

00:09:50.734 --> 00:09:52.167
You sure you don't want to
change it to Ronald?

00:09:52.167 --> 00:09:54.133
"Nah, nah. I want people to know
what they're getting

00:09:54.133 --> 00:09:55.901
when they walk in the door.

00:09:55.901 --> 00:09:57.200
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:00.033
Dr. Ronny.

00:10:00.033 --> 00:10:02.734
[ Normal voice ]
But let me see if I follow --
short temper, irritable,

00:10:02.734 --> 00:10:04.534
striking out
as a defense mechanism

00:10:04.534 --> 00:10:05.934
when they don't know
how to answer questions

00:10:05.934 --> 00:10:07.801
doesn't know what's going
on around them.

00:10:07.801 --> 00:10:09.901
I just wish there was an example
of someone prominent

00:10:09.901 --> 00:10:12.501
with those symptoms
who we could compare him to.

00:10:12.501 --> 00:10:15.400
It's just stumping me.
I mean, for the life of me,

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:18.100
I can't think of anyone
who's ever exhibited

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:20.434
these specific personality
traits before.

00:10:20.434 --> 00:10:24.067
I mean, certainly not someone
in the public eye,

00:10:24.067 --> 00:10:25.534
someone we all remember,

00:10:25.534 --> 00:10:28.501
you know, a businessman
or elected official,

00:10:28.501 --> 00:10:32.067
perhaps someone who served in
a high profile position within,

00:10:32.067 --> 00:10:34.200
I don't know, let's say,
the last 13 months,

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.200
if only that person existed?

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:40.501
Well,
I guess we'll never know.

00:10:42.501 --> 00:10:44.701
This is one of those
seemingly trivial moments

00:10:44.701 --> 00:10:46.667
that actually reveals
something fundamental

00:10:46.667 --> 00:10:48.467
at the heart
of modern Republican politics.

00:10:48.467 --> 00:10:50.434
In order to be
a successful Republican today,

00:10:50.434 --> 00:10:51.868
you simply have
to have no shame,

